course: dictionary
lesson: 1502
title: Cedar: a tree and its wood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which one you need. Cedar is one of these words. It can name a tall tree, or it can name the wood that comes from that tree.
explain: «A pencil is a rod of graphite mixed with clay, baked, laid in grooves between two thin slats of cedar wood, glued, cut and painted.» The sentence is about a pencil, and the word wood comes straight after cedar, so cedar means the wood. Test it: swap in "tree wood" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Ask yourself: is the sentence about a living plant, or about something made from it? A cedar growing on a hill is the tree. Cedar in a pencil is the wood.
fact: A cedar is a tall evergreen tree with needle-like leaves and cones, such as the cedar of Lebanon.
fact: Cedar wood is pleasant-smelling and reddish, and it is used for chests, fences and pencils.
fact: Cedar wood can keep moths away from clothes.
fact: Some other trees with sweet-smelling wood are also called cedars, for example western red cedar in Canada.
fact: Cedar appears on the flag of Lebanon, and the cedars of Lebanon are a symbol of strength and grandeur.
exercise: «The pencil is made with two slats of cedar wood.» In this sentence, what does cedar mean? | A pencil case | A kind of rock | A tall tree with cones | * The wood of cedar trees
exercise: In «two thin slats of cedar wood», which word after cedar tells you it means the material? | * wood | painted | glued | slats
exercise: «The cedar on the hill towered over the village.» What does cedar mean here? | * A tall evergreen tree | A pencil | A kind of moth | The reddish wood used for fences
test: Which of these is made from cedar wood, as the dictionary says? | A metal spoon | A plastic bottle | A glass window | * A fence
test: In «Some cedars have sweet-smelling wood», what does cedars mean? | Clothes | * Trees with sweet-smelling wood | Moths | Pencils
exam: Lena reads «A pencil is a rod of graphite mixed with clay, baked, laid in grooves between two thin slats of cedar wood.» Does cedar mean the tree or the wood? | The flag of Lebanon, because it is famous | The moth, because it eats the wood | The tree, because it grows in a forest | * The wood, because it is in a pencil and wood follows it
